# BNote Development Rules

## ⚠️ MOST IMPORTANT RULE - READ THIS FIRST ⚠️

**🚫 NEVER MODIFY ANY CODE OUTSIDE THE `/bnote-next-generation/` FOLDER 🚫**

**ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION:**
- ❌ **DO NOT** touch `/BNote/src/` directory (old PHP codebase)
- ❌ **DO NOT** modify `/BNote/main.php`, `/BNote/content.php`, or any files in `/BNote/` folder
- ❌ **DO NOT** change any files outside `/bnote-next-generation/` folder
- ❌ **DO NOT** refactor, update, modernize, or improve old codebase
- ❌ **DO NOT** fix bugs in old code (unless explicitly requested for critical security)
- ❌ **DO NOT** add features to old codebase
- ❌ **DO NOT** update dependencies for old codebase

**✅ ONLY ALLOWED:**
- ✅ Work **ONLY** in `/bnote-next-generation/` directory
- ✅ Modify files **ONLY** within `/bnote-next-generation/` folder
- ✅ Read old codebase for reference (but never modify)
- ✅ Use old codebase classes/functions via API calls (but never change them)
- ✅ Use `BNOTE_ROOT` constant (defined in `bnote-next-generation/api/paths.php`) to reference old codebase

**This is the #1 priority rule. If you're unsure, DON'T modify it. Ask the user first.**

## Project Context
This is BNote - an open source ensemble management system for bands, orchestras, and choirs.
- **Architecture:** 3-tier MVC (data/logic/presentation)
- **Old UI:** PHP-generated HTML with inline CSS (`/BNote/src/presentation/`) - **READ ONLY**
- **New UI:** BNote Next Generation - Next.js app in `frontend/` (`/bnote-next-generation/`) - **ONLY MODIFY THIS**
- **License:** GPL-3.0 (all code must remain GPL-compliant)

## Project Structure

```
/bnote/
├── BNote/                      ← Old codebase (NEVER MODIFY)
│   ├── src/
│   ├── main.php
│   └── config/
└── bnote-next-generation/      ← New app (ONLY MODIFY THIS)
    ├── api/
    ├── frontend/               ← Next.js UI (only UI)
    ├── lang/
    └── docs/
```

## Protected Directories (NEVER MODIFY)

**Complete list of off-limits directories:**
- `/BNote/src/` - All old PHP code (data, logic, presentation) - **READ ONLY**
- `/BNote/main.php` - Old entry point - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/content.php` - Old layout - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/index.php` - Old routing - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/components/` - Old JavaScript components - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/style/` - Old CSS/styles - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/lib/` - Old libraries - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- Any file or directory outside `/bnote-next-generation/` - **DO NOT TOUCH**

**Exception:** Only modify old code if user explicitly requests it for critical security fixes AND confirms in writing.

## Core Principles

### 1. Code Style (Next Generation Only)
- **Frontend:** TypeScript/React in `frontend/`; use English variable names (no German), meaningful names, consistent indentation; add comments for complex logic.
- **API:** PHP in `api/`; same naming and style principles.

### 2. Browser Compatibility
- Target modern browsers (last 2 versions)
- No IE11 support needed
- Progressive enhancement approach
- Use standard HTML5/CSS3

### 3. Internationalization (i18n) - MANDATORY

**CRITICAL:** ALL user-facing strings MUST use the i18n system. No hardcoded text.

**For Next Generation UI (`frontend/`):**
- **React/TSX:** Use the i18n context `t(key)` for all user-facing strings (e.g. `t("js.dashboard.welcome")`).
- **Translation Files:** Add keys to all language files (`bnote-next-generation/lang/*.json`).
- **Key Format:** `js.{module}.{key}` (e.g., `js.dashboard.welcome`).
- **Never hardcode:** No user-facing strings in code; use translation keys.
- **German text:** Only in `bnote-next-generation/lang/de.json` (translation file).

**Examples:**
```tsx
// GOOD
<h1>{t("js.dashboard.welcome")}</h1>
<input placeholder={t("js.login.usernamePlaceholder")} />
showToast(t("js.users.created"));

// BAD
<h1>Welcome</h1>
showToast('User created');
```

### 4. Dark Mode Support - MANDATORY

**CRITICAL:** ALL UI components MUST support dark mode.

**CSS Variables:**
- Use semantic color variables from `frontend/app/globals.css` (e.g. `var(--background)`, `var(--foreground)`, `var(--primary)`)
- Variables adapt to dark mode via theme class/attribute
- Never hardcode colors

**Tailwind Classes:**
```html
<!-- GOOD - Uses semantic variables -->
<div class="bg-background text-foreground">
  <div class="bg-card border border-border">
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">Text</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- BAD - Hardcoded colors -->
<div class="bg-white text-black dark:bg-gray-800 dark:text-white">
```

**Theme Toggle:**
- Theme toggle component in `frontend/components/ThemeToggle.tsx`; preference saved in localStorage; respects system preference on first load.

**Testing:**
- Always test components in both light and dark modes
- Use browser dev tools to toggle dark mode

### 5. Shared Components Architecture - MANDATORY

**CRITICAL:** Build shared, reusable components that are used throughout the app. Do NOT create duplicate implementations.

**Key Principles:**
- ✅ **Extract common functionality** into shared components/modules
- ✅ **Reuse existing components** instead of creating new ones
- ✅ **Share design/styling** through shared rendering components
- ✅ **No dependencies** between feature modules (e.g., Search should not depend on Dashboard)
- ✅ **Shared utilities** for common operations (formatting, rendering, etc.)

**Examples:**

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Shared EventCard / event-utils
// frontend/components/EventCard.tsx, frontend/lib/event-utils.ts
// Dashboard and Search use same components/utilities; no cross-module dependencies.
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD - Duplicate implementations in different pages
// Each page implementing its own event card rendering instead of using EventCard.
```

**When to Create Shared Components:**
- When the same functionality appears in 2+ places
- When rendering logic is shared (e.g., event cards, user cards)
- When formatting/utility functions are reused
- When design consistency is required across modules

**Shared Component Structure:**
- Place in `frontend/components/` or `frontend/lib/` with descriptive names (e.g. `EventCard.tsx`, `event-utils.ts`)
- Include GPL v3 license header where applicable
- Export components and utilities for use across pages
- Support required options (mobile/desktop, participation widgets, etc.)

**Architectural Independence:**
- Pages (dashboard, search, contacts, etc.) should NOT depend on each other
- They SHOULD use shared components and lib utilities (e.g. EventCard, entity-config, event-utils)

### 6. License Compliance

- All code must remain GPL-3.0
- **MANDATORY:** Add GPL v3 license headers to all source files in `/next/`
- Use standard Tailwind patterns (MIT licensed)
- Avoid copying proprietary UI components
- Keep GPL headers in all modified files

## Next Generation UI Development

**Location:** `/bnote-next-generation/` directory ONLY; **UI code:** `frontend/` (Next.js)

**Key Requirements:**
1. **MANDATORY i18n:** All user-facing strings must use `t(key)` from i18n context (`lang/*.json` keys)
2. **MANDATORY Dark Mode:** All components must use semantic CSS variables from `frontend/app/globals.css`
3. **MANDATORY Shared Components:** Reuse components in `frontend/components/` and lib in `frontend/lib/`; avoid duplicate implementations
4. **GPL Headers:** All source files must include GPL v3 license headers where applicable
5. **API:** Use API client in `frontend/lib/api.ts`; backend is module-based (`api/index.php?module=X&action=Y`)
6. **Translation Files:** Add keys to all `bnote-next-generation/lang/*.json` files
7. **Path Configuration:** API uses `BNOTE_ROOT` from `bnote-next-generation/api/paths.php` to reference BNote codebase
8. **Architectural Independence:** Pages should not depend on each other, only on shared components and lib

**Technology Stack:**
- Next.js (static export), React, TypeScript in `frontend/`
- Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons
- I18n via context and `lang/*.json`; theme toggle in `frontend/components/ThemeToggle.tsx`

**See:** [bnote-next-generation/README.md](bnote-next-generation/README.md) and [docs/FEATURES_AND_BEHAVIORS.md](bnote-next-generation/docs/FEATURES_AND_BEHAVIORS.md)

## Workflow

**For Next Generation UI (`/bnote-next-generation/`):**
1. All user-facing strings must use i18n
2. All components must support dark mode
3. Extract shared functionality into reusable components (no duplicate implementations)
4. Feature modules should be independent (no cross-dependencies, only shared components)
5. Use semantic CSS variables for colors
6. Test in both light and dark modes
7. Add translation keys to all language files
8. Add GPL v3 headers to all new/modified files

## Next Generation UI Examples

### Example: Component with i18n and Dark Mode

```tsx
// GOOD - Uses t() and semantic CSS variables
<div className="rounded-lg p-4" style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--card)', borderColor: 'var(--border)', borderWidth: 1 }}>
    <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold mb-4" style={{ color: 'var(--card-foreground)' }}>{t("js.dashboard.welcome")}</h2>
    <p style={{ color: 'var(--muted-foreground)' }}>{t("js.dashboard.subtitle").replace("%p", company)}</p>
    <button className="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-white" style={{ background: 'var(--primary)' }}>{t("js.common.save")}</button>
</div>
```

## Priority Order

**Next Generation:**
1. Complete localization for existing modules
2. Implement remaining modules (Calendar, Messages, etc.)
3. Add advanced features (search, exports, etc.)

## Testing Reminders

- Test in Chrome/Firefox (latest)
- Check mobile responsiveness (narrow browser window)
- Verify all buttons/links still work
- No JavaScript errors in console
- Forms still submit correctly
- Test in both light and dark modes

## Notes

- Cursor should generate clean, readable code
- Preserve existing functionality 100%
- For Next Generation: Always use i18n and support dark mode
- **NEVER modify old codebase** - work only in `/bnote-next-generation/` directory
